  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, thanks for reporting this. I checked and the second-floor printer (BL-PR-FL2) is offline for everyone, so the problem is the printer itself and not your computer. Could you or someone near it try these steps? 1) Look at the printer's screen for any error, like a paper jam, no paper or toner, or an open door, and clear it. 2) Turn the printer off, wait 30 seconds, then turn it back on. 3) Make sure the network cable at the back is plugged in firmly and its link light is on. Then reply to let me know what the screen showed and whether it comes back online. I'll check it from here and we can print a test page. If it's still offline after the restart, I'll send it to our second-level team. In the meantime, the first-floor printer (BL-PR-FL1) is working. To add it, go to Settings > Bluetooth & devices > Printers & scanners > Add device. If it isn't listed, choose \"Add manually\" and enter BL-PR-FL1.",
  "internal_note": "Sender: James O'Connor (user_id 8), Ops Warehouse Supervisor, account active, device BL-DT-0108. BL-PR-FL2 status check: online=false, no warnings, last check-in 2026-10-09T09:54:57Z (about 5 hours before BL-PR-FL1's last check-in). Per KB-022 this is a printer-side fault, not the user's PC. I asked the user for an on-site check of the panel error, a 30-second power cycle, and the network cable/link light. Gave BL-PR-FL1 (online, no warnings) as a fallback per KB-024. Next step: when the user replies, re-check BL-PR-FL2. If it is still offline after a power cycle with no error shown, escalate to Tier 2 per KB-022 (possible network or hardware fault).",
